alse","unknown"]}},"required":["conditionId","value"],"additionalProperties":false}},"effect":{"type":"string","enum":["reachable","blocked","unknown"]},"explanation":{"type":"string"},"missingFacts":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}},"factIds":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}}},"required":["id","assumptions","effect","explanation","missingFacts","factIds"],"additionalProperties":false}}},"required":["obligationId","explanation","facts","decisiveMissingFacts","suggestedObservations","decision","branchResults"],"additionalProperties":false}}},"required":["results"],"additionalProperties":false}]},"usage":{"input":5606,"output":1312,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0},"costUsd":null,"transportAttempts":"unknown","response":{"text":"","toolCalls":[{"id":"call_DuxZxu5fqN7zXBpIj717zs49","name":"submit_authorization_result","arguments":{"results":[{"obligationId":"scenario%3Atoken-status-unspecified::entry%3Aget-shared","decision":{"kind":"conditional-policy","policyStatus":"undetermined"},"branchResults":[],"explanation":"At the declared GetSharedMemo entry, the source-visible path first resolves the supplied token as an active memo share. If lookup returns no share or the share is expired, the handler returns NOT_FOUND. If lookup returns an unexpired share, the handler binds the resource to the share's MemoID, fetches that exact memo, rejects a missing, non-active, or SPACE memo, and then evaluates the read context with that same shared memo ID. The decisive authorization control is the shared-token binding in CheckMemoReadContext: when the memo ID equals the shared memo ID and the memo is not SpaceAudience, the read decision is allowed as private, before the ordinary anonymous/private-memo denial path. Thus, under the stated premise that a resolving token's memo is active, private, non-SPACE, and has a valid creator, the valid-token branch is source-visible as retrieval allowed, while invalid or expired tokens are source-visible as NOT_FOUND. The current scenario remains undetermined because the supplied facts do not establish whether the token lookup returns a share or whether the returned share is unexpired. No separate requested memo identity is introduced: the protected memo is selected from the token's MemoID. Deployment behavior and repository-wide completeness are not inferred.","facts":[{"id":"entry-get-shared","kind":"entry","statement":"GetSharedMemo is an unauthenticated entry that begins by resolving the supplied share token.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-e4f8cd24172048ad","startLine":170,"endLine":173}]},{"id":"identity-anonymous","kind":"binding","statement":"The read context obtains the current viewer; when no viewer exists, anonymous access handling is used, and the context is built with the supplied shared memo ID.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-4715f0667b50b99d","startLine":17,"endLine":29}]},{"id":"resource-token-memo-binding","kind":"binding","statement":"After a successful share lookup, the handler retrieves the memo using the share record's MemoID, so the token selects the protected memo.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-e4f8cd24172048ad","startLine":178,"endLine":186}]},{"id":"control-token-validity","kind":"control","statement":"A missing share or an expired share produces NOT_FOUND; otherwise the active share is returned for continued processing.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-e4f8cd24172048ad","startLine":217,"endLine":229}]},{"id":"control-shared-access","kind":"control","statement":"The strongest visible authorization control grants a private read decision when the shared memo ID matches the memo ID and the memo is not a SPACE memo.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-5680870821a0e984","startLine":119,"endLine":121}]},{"id":"control-handler-check","kind":"control","statement":"The handler rejects the request with NOT_FOUND when read-context construction fails or the resulting memo-read decision is not allowed.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-e4f8cd24172048ad","startLine":186,"endLine":188}]},{"id":"effect-invalid-or-inaccessible","kind":"effect","statement":"Missing, non-active, or SPACE memos are returned as NOT_FOUND, and invalid or expired token resolution also returns NOT_FOUND.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-e4f8cd24172048ad","startLine":182,"endLine":188}]},{"id":"effect-valid-token","kind":"effect","statement":"On the valid-token path, the converted memo is returned and its parent relation is cleared, limiting the grant to the exact token-associated memo.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-e4f8cd24172048ad","startLine":203,"endLine":213}]},{"id":"condition-token-status","kind":"condition","statement":"Whether the supplied token resolves to a share and whether that share is unexpired are not established by the supplied task facts.","citations":[{"sourceId":"src-e4f8cd24172048ad","startLine":221,"endLine":229}]}],"decisiveMissingFacts":["Whether Store.GetMemoShare finds a share record for the supplied token.","If a share record is found, whether isMemoShareExpired evaluates to false for that record at runtime."],"suggestedObservations":["Observe the result of getActiveMemoShare for the supplied token: whether it returns a non-nil share or NOT_FOUND, and, if non-nil, whether its expiry test is false.","Observe the resolved share's MemoID and confirm that the fetched memo is the associated active, private, non-SPACE memo assumed by the task."]}]}}],"tokens":{"input":5606,"output":1312,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0},"costUsd":null,"durationMs":36495.94,"stopReason":"tool_use"},"schemaValidation":{"valid":true,"diagnostics":[]},"endedAt":"2026-09-29T19:11:52.155Z"}}
